WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.345
Lesson 6.6.

00:00:02.345 --> 00:00:06.001
Vote-escrow tokenomics, bribes and governance markets.

00:00:06.001 --> 00:00:08.657
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:12.577
to understand vote-escrow ("ve") systems and bribe markets, a

00:00:12.577 --> 00:00:14.916
major source of DeFi yield and power.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.506
Here's the plan.

00:00:17.506 --> 00:00:19.191
First, the key ideas.

00:00:19.191 --> 00:00:21.906
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:21.906 --> 00:00:23.431
Then, your checklist.

00:00:23.431 --> 00:00:25.593
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:30.580
First, Vote-escrow: you lock a governance token for a

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.789
period (often up to 4 years) and get ve-tokens

00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:37.845
with voting power that decays as the unlock approaches.

00:00:37.845 --> 00:00:39.930
Longer lock = more power.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.546
Next, Gauges: ve-holders vote on which

00:00:42.546 --> 00:00:45.865
pools receive the protocol's token emissions.

00:00:45.865 --> 00:00:49.205
Emissions attract liquidity, so votes are valuable.

00:00:49.205 --> 00:00:52.612
Then, Bribes / voting incentives: protocols that want

00:00:52.612 --> 00:00:55.940
liquidity pay ve-holders to vote for their pool.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.016
Voters earn this as yield (plus a

00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:00.208
share of fees in some designs).

00:01:00.208 --> 00:01:04.264
Also, Liquid lockers / meta-governance: protocols that lock on

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:07.268
your behalf and give you a tradable token.

00:01:07.268 --> 00:01:09.152
It's liquid, but it can trade at a

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:11.498
discount, and it adds a layer of risk.

00:01:11.498 --> 00:01:14.061
And finally, Risks: long locks (you can't

00:01:14.061 --> 00:01:16.501
sell), the token's price over the lock,

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:19.613
emissions diluting holders, and governance capture.

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:23.428
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:23.428 --> 00:01:28.688
$10,000 of a ve-token earning ~15% APR in

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:34.373
bribes ≈ $1,500/yr, paid in various tokens.

00:01:34.373 --> 00:01:37.440
But the underlying is locked for 4 years:

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.360
if the token falls 60%, the position is

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.508
worth $4,000 plus the bribes collected.

00:01:43.508 --> 00:01:46.782
A liquid-locker version lets you exit, but it traded

00:01:46.782 --> 00:01:49.738
at a 20% discount during the last sell-off.

00:01:49.738 --> 00:01:52.293
Price the lock, not just the APR.

00:01:53.593 --> 00:01:55.053
Here's your checklist.

00:01:55.053 --> 00:01:56.588
Do it now, for real.

00:01:56.588 --> 00:01:59.223
First, Lock length and decay understood.

00:01:59.223 --> 00:02:02.958
Next, Bribe income valued at a realistic sale price.

00:02:02.958 --> 00:02:07.128
And finally, Liquid-locker discount history checked before using one.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.638
Question 1.

00:02:09.638 --> 00:02:11.253
What do ve-holders vote on?

00:02:15.673 --> 00:02:18.217
The answer: Which pools receive emissions

00:02:18.217 --> 00:02:21.063
(gauge weights) and other governance decisions.

00:02:22.363 --> 00:02:23.608
Question 2.

00:02:23.608 --> 00:02:25.433
Why do protocols pay bribes?

00:02:29.853 --> 00:02:31.963
The answer: Votes direct emissions

00:02:31.963 --> 00:02:34.193
to their pools, attracting liquidity.

00:02:35.493 --> 00:02:36.763
Question 3.

00:02:36.763 --> 00:02:38.543
Main cost of a 4-year lock?

00:02:42.963 --> 00:02:45.043
The answer: You can't sell during the

00:02:45.043 --> 00:02:47.123
lock, whatever the token's price does.

00:02:48.423 --> 00:02:49.668
Let's recap.

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:53.302
Vote-escrow: you lock a governance token for a period

00:02:53.302 --> 00:02:56.330
(often up to 4 years) and get ve-tokens with

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.995
voting power that decays as the unlock approaches.

00:02:59.995 --> 00:03:02.473
Gauges: ve-holders vote on which pools

00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:05.250
receive the protocol's token emissions.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.857
Bribes / voting incentives: protocols that want liquidity

00:03:08.857 --> 00:03:11.520
pay ve-holders to vote for their pool.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.685
Liquid lockers / meta-governance.

00:03:14.984 --> 00:03:17.499
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:17.499 --> 00:03:20.311
Next up, Lesson 6.7: Valuing DeFi

00:03:20.311 --> 00:03:24.364
protocols: fees, revenue, earnings and multiples.
